    "answer": {
      "short": "To the right by $\\frac12$ unit.",
      "worked": "Bob translates right 1 unit, then replaces $x$ by $2x$ for the horizontal dilation:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(x-1)\\\\y&=f(2x-1).\\end{align*}$$\nMary’s dilation gives $y=f(2x)$. Translating right $\\frac12$ unit gives\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f\\left(2\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)\\right)\\\\y&=f(2x-1),\\end{align*}$$\nwhich matches Bob’s graph.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
